# MageRide — ignored paths. Extended by C001 (repo-scaffold).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
*.user
*.suo
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coverisxml
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
.dotnet/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / Next.js (portals)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
.turbo/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
coverage/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradle / Android / KMP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
# ...but the top-level build/ is the MageRide build plan (manifest, prompts, progress),
# not a Gradle output directory.
!/build/
# C001 redirects the root project's buildDir to .gradle/root-build, but that override only
# takes effect once the root project is evaluated. A configuration failure earlier than that
# (a build-script compile error, for example) still drops Gradle's problems report into the
# default location — which is the build plan. Re-ignore the directories Gradle owns so a
# stray report can never be committed alongside the manifest. (C011)
/build/reports/
/build/tmp/
/build/kotlin/
# The Gradle wrapper is committed on purpose — never add a blanket *.jar rule above it.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
local.properties
.kotlin/
.cxx/
captures/
*.hprof
*.klib
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iOS / Xcode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
Pods/
.swiftpm/
Carthage/Build/
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets, keys and local environment
# `.env.*.example` templates (D7 §4, created by C009) stay tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
!*.example
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.*.json
# Self-signed dev TLS material generated by infra/scripts/dev-up.sh for HAProxy (C009).
infra/deploy/certs/
# The device CA dev-up.sh generates for the hardware-tracker plane (C030, T-02). Its root
# key mints a working credential for any vehicle, so it never goes in the repository — EMQX
# and provisioning-svc both mount the directory instead.
infra/deploy/device-ca/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
